### What I learned
    - scalar function creation : 
               1)Central registry that maps function name -> function creators in src/Functions/FunctionFactory.h
               2)Whatever function you're creating should inherit from IFunction.h
               3)MyFunc.cpp -> in the end you have to register using REGISTER_FUNCTIO(MyFunc){
                         factory.registerFunction<FunctionMyFunc>();
               }   macro
               4)  Methods that has to be overriden : getName(),getNumberOfArguements(),  getReturnTypeImpl() , executeImpl()->main logic
               
     - Aggregate function creation :
               1)  src/AggregateFunctions/
                    ├── AggregateFunctionFactory.h      ← Registry
                    ├── IAggregateFunction.h            ← Base interface
                    ├── registerAggregateFunctions.cpp  ← Registration
                    ├── AggregateFunctionAvg.h/.cpp     ← Example
                    ├── AggregateFunctionGroupPolygonUnion.h/.cpp  ← Your function!
                    └── ...
                2)Usually in .h files 
                        file - Logic
                        Class definition
                        Data struct (state),  add(), merge(), serialize(), deserialize(), insertResultInto()
                    and .cpp files
                        file - Registration
                        #include the .h file
                        Factory function (createAggregateFunctionXXX)
                        registerAggregateFunctionXXX() function

                    src/AggregateFunctions/
                    ├── AggregateFunctionGroupPolygonUnion.h    ← Logic (class + methods) it uses CRTP pattern
                    ├── AggregateFunctionGroupPolygonUnion.cpp  ← Registration only
                    └── registerAggregateFunctions.cpp          ← Declarations + calls

                3) Then in src/AggregateFunctions/registerAggregateFunctions.cpp:
                    // Line 23: Declaration
                    void registerAggregateFunctionGroupPolygonUnion(AggregateFunctionFactory &);
                    // Line 135: Call
                    registerAggregateFunctionGroupPolygonUnion(factory);

                4) These methods has to be implemented by the Aggregate function class
                        +---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
                        | Component                 | Purpose                                                      |
                        +---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
                        | Data struct               | Defines state (e.g., {sum, count})                            |
                        | getName()                 | Returns the SQL function name                                 |
                        | add()                     | Processes each row and updates the state                      |
                        | merge()                   | Combines states from parallel threads                         |
                        | serialize()               | Saves state for distributed queries                           |
                        | deserialize()             | Loads state from distributed queries                          |
                        | insertResultInto()        | Extracts final result from the state                          |
                        | allocatesMemoryInArena()  | Indicates whether the function allocates memory in Arena      |
                        |                           | true  → Uses Arena for dynamic allocations (strings, arrays)  |
                        |                           | false → Uses only fixed-size state                            |
                        +---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+



